# Defining an Interface 📋

An `interface` describes the shape of an object:

```typescript
interface UserProfile {
  id: number;
  username: string;
  email: string;
  isActive: boolean;
}

const user: UserProfile = {
  id: 101,
  username: "marcus_dev",
  email: "marcus@example.com",
  isActive: true
};

console.log(`User ${user.username} loaded with ID ${user.id}`);
```

