# Methods and Callable Interfaces 📞

Declare methods and callable function signatures:

```typescript
interface MathCalculator {
  version: string;
  calculate(a: number, b: number): number;
}

const adder: MathCalculator = {
  version: "1.0.0",
  calculate(x, y) {
    return x + y;
  }
};

console.log("Result:", adder.calculate(15, 25));
```

<!-- FULL_CODE_START
interface MathCalculator {
  version: string;
  calculate(a: number, b: number): number;
}

const adder: MathCalculator = {
  version: "1.0.0",
  calculate: (x, y) => x + y
};

console.log("Calculator version:", adder.version);
console.log("15 + 25 =", adder.calculate(15, 25));
FULL_CODE_END -->

# Combining Types: Intersections (`&`) 🔀

Combine multiple types into a unified type that satisfies **all** properties:

```typescript
type HasName = { name: string };
type HasAge = { age: number };
type HasPermissions = { role: "admin" | "user" };

// Intersection of all three types
type SystemAdmin = HasName & HasAge & HasPermissions;

const adminUser: SystemAdmin = {
  name: "Marcus",
  age: 34,
  role: "admin"
};

console.log("Admin User:", adminUser);
```

