# Hybrid Types (Callable & Object Properties) 🔀

In JavaScript, functions can also have properties attached to them:

```typescript
interface CounterFunction {
  (): number;      // Callable function signature
  reset(): void;   // Method on the function
  count: number;   // Property on the function
}

function getCounter(): CounterFunction {
  const fn = function() {
    return ++fn.count;
  } as CounterFunction;

  fn.count = 0;
  fn.reset = function() { fn.count = 0; };
  return fn;
}

const counter = getCounter();
console.log(counter()); // 1
console.log(counter()); // 2
counter.reset();
console.log("After reset:", counter()); // 1
```

