# Implementing Interfaces with Classes 🏛️

Classes can enforce that they adhere to an interface using `implements`:

```typescript
interface Authenticable {
  authenticate(token: string): boolean;
}

class UserSession implements Authenticable {
  constructor(private validToken: string) {}

  authenticate(token: string): boolean {
    return token === this.validToken;
  }
}

const session = new UserSession("SECRET_123");
console.log("Auth check:", session.authenticate("SECRET_123"));
```

